# Microsoft-confidential dossier — never in git (NDA-split, installed into ~/.roberdan-os/private/)
private/

# Kanban card CONTENT is Roberto's live operational/business state (task detail, client/product
# specifics) — local-only, never committed. The tool itself (kb.sh, README.md) stays versioned;
# only the data directories are ignored. Purged from history 2026-07-04 (see CHANGELOG).
kanban/todo/
kanban/doing/
kanban/done/

# The nested private card repo. `kanban/` holds 69 cards with real names and
# clients; the card DIRECTORIES above are excluded because this remote is
# PUBLIC. The nested repo that versions them lives in loco (kb.sh:43-61
# documents what happened the last time cards were addressed through
# RDA_KANBAN: the writes landed on the wrong board). Its .git and its own
# ignore file are bookkeeping for THAT repo and must never be offered to this
# one - untracked here means a stray `git add` cannot reach them.
kanban/.git/
kanban/.gitignore

# OS / editor
.DS_Store
*.swp
.idea/
.vscode/

# Loop cursor state (durable, not versioned)
.agent-state/

# Per-platform wrappers — fully generated by `bin/sync.sh --emit-only` from the canon.
# Run it locally whenever you need them on disk; test/validate.sh checks generation is
# deterministic instead of diffing against a committed copy. See bin/sync.sh, README.md.
platforms/

# claude-ai-skill/ zip is a build artifact of the committed roberto-mode/ source folder —
# regenerate with `cd claude-ai-skill && zip -r roberto-mode.zip roberto-mode`.
claude-ai-skill/*.zip

# eval/ harness output — generated by eval/run-eval.sh, eval/judge.sh, eval/report.sh.
# Regenerate on demand; see eval/README.md. Commit a specific eval/results/report.md by hand
# (force-add) if you want to keep a dated snapshot.
eval/results/
.gstack/

# Build artifact — regenerate with the make-pdf skill against docs/roberdan-os-paper-en.md.
docs/*.pdf
.gbrain-source

# Pause/resume checkpoint — ephemeral local runtime state, per-repo (see kb pause/resume).
handoff/resume.md

# Serena (coding-agent toolkit) per-machine project config. Scaffolded on its own
# the first time a session touches this repo with Serena's MCP enabled - it appeared
# untracked mid-run on 2026-07-28 without anyone asking for it. Machine-local tool
# state, not repo canon: an unreviewed config landing in a commit by accident is
# exactly what `git add -A` (already blocked by the pre-commit hook) would do.
# Force-add it by hand if this repo ever deliberately adopts Serena.
.serena/
